  "notes": [
    "Source: the server is @modelcontextprotocol/server-everything 2026.8.31 (serverInfo 2.0.0). Every tool, resource, prompt and completion is computed in handlers.py from recorded behavior; the package's published source was read (never executed or called) as documentation to explain recorded behavior.",
    "Conditional tools: trigger-sampling-request-async needs sampling + tasks.requests.sampling.createMessage, trigger-elicitation-request-async needs elicitation + tasks.requests.elicitation.create (server source; recordings confirm a sampling-only client is not offered it). Introspection only saw them with every capability at once.",
    "Dynamic resource timestamps use JavaScript toLocaleTimeString() in the server's local zone; recorded at 01:40Z showing 9:40 PM, i.e. UTC-4 in October: modeled as America/New_York.",
    "gzip-file-as-resource: the fake never fetches http(s) URLs. The default README URL serves the recorded bytes (recorded 2026-10-14); any other http(s) URL answers 'fetch failed', as the real server does when the network fails. data: URIs are decoded and gzipped exactly (byte-identical to Node's zlib for the recorded inputs).",
    "get-roots-list without an open GET stream: the real server's roots/list request goes unanswered and the call returns after the SDK's 60 s timeout; the fake pauses 60 s (skipped in fast mode).",
    "Protocol negotiation: the SDK (types.js SUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSIONS, LATEST_PROTOCOL_VERSION) echoes a supported version (incl. 2024-10-07, listed in the recorded 400 for a bad version header) and answers anything else with 2025-11-25. The recorder can't send a second initialize in a session, so this comes from the source, not a recording."
  ]
